>> title: Chile Verde, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: pork, tomatillo, chiles, mexican, braise, tacos, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: chile-verde
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: chile verde, puerco en salsa verde, green chile pork, chili verde, pork chile verde, slow cooker chile verde, crockpot chile verde
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, mexican-red-rice
>> servings: 8
>> time: 8 hr 45 min
>> slack: forgiving — the sauce goes from bright green to dull olive whatever you do, and that is the dish rather than a fault
>> step.2: char under the broiler 12 min, peel
>> step.3: blend with the cilantro
>> step.4: brown 10 min in a skillet, in batches
>> step.5: braise on low, 8 hr
>> step.6: reduce uncovered on high 20 min, then lime

Written for low, eight hours. Two ovens' worth of colour happen before the machine is switched on — the chiles under the broiler and the pork in a skillet — and then nothing is asked of you until evening. The stock halves, to one cup: tomatillos are mostly water and all of it stays in the pot.

Char @tomatillos{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; husked), @poblano chiles{3}, @Anaheim chiles{2}, @jalapeños{2}, @white onion{1%large}(quartered), @garlic{6%cloves}(unpeeled) under a #broiler{} for ~toast{12%min}, turning once, until the skins blacken — then steam them covered and slip the skins off the poblanos.

Blend @&(~1)charred vegetables{} with @cilantro{1%cup}(leaves and stems), @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried Mexican oregano{1%tsp}, @chicken stock{1%cup}(240 mL) to a loose green sauce.

Brown @pork shoulder{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1 1/2-in cubes) seasoned with @kosher salt{1%Tbs} in @lard{2%Tbs} in a #skillet{} for ~sear{10%min}, in batches with room around every piece.

Slow cook @&(~1)browned pork{} under @&(~2)tomatillo sauce{} in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{8%hr}, lid on, the skillet scraped out into the pot so the fond goes in with it.

Finish @&(~1)chile verde{} uncovered on high for ~reduce{20%min}, until it is a sauce that clings rather than a green broth, and stir in @fresh lime juice{1%Tbs} off the heat.
